es what the grisella what your question  of the aircraft dispute is concerned of  the normal dispute of  the aircraft topic there  i i think i mentioned that we have  installed a  working group um that is  detailing out and discussing on the  case-by-case level  uh whether the level playing field is  kept  or whether there are state aid issues so  it's a very practical approach  that has been chosen and you see there  was a strong will  really to solve that issue what your  second question is concerned if i got it  right  you were asking about the overall  financial  support here i think two  figures are interesting we have been  looking at  what is the fiscal support of the  european union on the european level  of course the member states level and  what we call the automatic  stabilizers in the european union for  the years 20 21 and 22  this will sum up around about to 18  percent of our gdp  and if you compare that with the same  levels in the  uh united states and the plans  that have been launched  by president biden or announced by  president biden  and you some sum it up over the three  years you come to a result of  20 percent of gdp so that shows  that we're pretty much aligned uh in our  policies  and that we share the same approach  that right now we should not  pull out prematurely pull out of the  supportive measures we should not repeat  the mistakes of the last  big financial crisis but we should  maintain  the fiscal support also through 22  knowing that policies then have to be  more differentiated so to prepare  for the years to come where the fiscal  support will be reduced  i'll take one more question from the  room beda  please  yes good afternoon veda romanus i had a  question to mrs van der lion  um you met mr biden uh  for a number of days from friday onwards  um did you have the possibility of  explaining to him  the concept of european sovereignty  of strategic autonomy  and did he ask you more information  about these two concepts  and w